# .env.example — starter environment file for projects adopting claude_template_yaml.
#
# Copy this to .env (gitignored) and fill in the values. The Strategist owns
# this file — values are confirmed during the first-contact interview, per
# docs/dev_framework/strategist.md §"First-contact interview".
#
# .env is the canonical source of truth for machine-readable project variables.
# CLAUDE.md displays the same values inline for human readers — keep them in
# sync. Scripts (setup_dev_slots.sh, future helpers) source this file rather
# than parsing CLAUDE.md, so values here are what tooling actually sees.
#
# Lines marked PLACEHOLDER must be replaced before scripts that consume them
# will run. setup_dev_slots.sh halts on PLACEHOLDER values for PROJECT_SUB
# and PROJECT_PORTS (per FWADR-019 Revision v1.1).
#
# LAUNCH: this file must be in Claude Code's process env at launch — MCP
# credentials and the git-auth block below bind from the process env, not from
# the file itself. Launch via the claude-env / claude-env-yolo shell functions
# (FWADR-032; snippet at docs/dev_framework/_stubs/shell/claude-env.zsh).
# Sessions launched bare get a session-start NOTICE until relaunched.

# =============================================================================
# Project identity
# =============================================================================

# Project name (machine-safe slug; lowercase, hyphens or underscores OK).
# Example: PROJECT_NAME=auto-portal
PROJECT_NAME=PLACEHOLDER

# Project subdomain — the <sub> in URLs like <slot>.<sub>.localhost (dev) and
# <sub>.<website>.com (prod). Short, lowercase.
# Example: PROJECT_SUB=auto
PROJECT_SUB=PLACEHOLDER

# Parent domain — the <website> in <sub>.<website>.com. Bare domain, no scheme.
# Example: PROJECT_WEBSITE=jumpermedia.co
PROJECT_WEBSITE=PLACEHOLDER

# Port range allocated to this project — used by setup_dev_slots.sh to pick
# slot ports and (if HTTP surface) configure Caddy reverse-proxy blocks.
# Format: <low>-<high>. Need at least 4 contiguous ports for dev slots.
# Strategist confirms with the user to avoid collisions with other projects
# on the same machine. Example: PROJECT_PORTS=3050-3060
PROJECT_PORTS=PLACEHOLDER

# Dev environment mode — local-hosted (dev on user's machine) or
# remote-hosted (dev on a shared server). See docs/architecture/adr-011-dev-environment.md
# once that ADR is accepted.
# Example: DEV_ENVIRONMENT_MODE=local-hosted
DEV_ENVIRONMENT_MODE=PLACEHOLDER

# Git host — where this project's repo(s) are stored. The framework's git
# policy is host-neutral ("PR" means pull request / merge request on whatever
# host this names); this variable is what tells agents which host CLI and MCP
# to reach for, and where new repos get created. Ask the user — never assume.
#   github  → github.com; host CLI is `gh`; github MCP applies
#   gitlab  → GitLab (self-hosted or gitlab.com); host CLI is `glab`
#   other   → record the workflow in dev_framework_exceptions.md
# Example: GIT_HOST=gitlab
GIT_HOST=PLACEHOLDER

# Base URL of the git host — required when GIT_HOST is self-hosted (e.g. a
# private GitLab or GitHub Enterprise). Include scheme, no trailing slash.
# Leave unset for github.com / gitlab.com.
# Example: GIT_HOST_URL=https://gitlab.internal.example.com
# GIT_HOST_URL=

# Host API token (PAT) — lets git push/pull over HTTPS with no SSH key, and
# authenticates the host CLI. Set the ONE matching GIT_HOST; the auto-wire block
# at the bottom of this file routes git to the host's credential helper with it
# (FWADR-030). Create a PAT with read/write repo scope on the host. Keep it here
# (.env is gitignored), never in a committed file.
#   github → GH_TOKEN        (GitHub Enterprise: use GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN instead)
#   gitlab → GITLAB_TOKEN    (same var for gitlab.com and self-hosted)
# GH_TOKEN=
# GITLAB_TOKEN=

# =============================================================================
# Split layout (FWADR-021)
# =============================================================================

# Name of the subdirectory holding the primary code repo. Matches the repo
# slug on the git host exactly. Used by the Developer (cd $PROJECT_DIR/$DEFAULT_CODE_SUBDIR
# at bootstrap) and by sync-framework.sh (subdir .env scan fallback).
# Example: DEFAULT_CODE_SUBDIR=auto-jm-co
DEFAULT_CODE_SUBDIR=PLACEHOLDER

# Path to the canonical claude_template_yaml repo on this machine. Optional —
# if unset, sync-framework.sh falls back to sibling-directory search
# (../claude_template_yaml, ../../claude_template_yaml, ../../../claude_template_yaml).
# Example: CLAUDE_TEMPLATE_ROOT=/Users/you/code/claude_template_yaml
# CLAUDE_TEMPLATE_ROOT=

# =============================================================================
# Worker spawning (FWADR-031, macOS)
# =============================================================================
# scripts/spawn_worker.sh <name> ["prompt"] opens a new terminal at the project,
# sources this .env, and launches a named, Remote-Control-enabled Claude worker
# (drivable from your phone). Set which terminal app it opens. Default: iterm.
#   iterm    → iTerm2
#   terminal → macOS Terminal.app
# WORKER_TERMINAL=iterm

# =============================================================================
# Researcher role (optional — FWADR-024)
# =============================================================================
# Fill ONLY if this project activates the Researcher role ("you are the
# Researcher"). The role refuses to bootstrap while these are unset, and
# scripts/check-researcher-scope.sh (the pre-merge write-fence check) exits 2.
# The human-readable half of the parameter surface (intake, gap surfaces,
# doctrine reading list) lives in dev_framework_exceptions.md — see
# docs/dev_framework/researcher.md §"Parameter surface".

# The ONE directory (relative to $CODE_ROOT) the Researcher may modify.
# Example: RESEARCHER_SCOPE_DIR=ingress
# RESEARCHER_SCOPE_DIR=

# Optional comma-separated exact file paths outside the scope dir the
# Researcher may also edit (data files, not code — e.g. resolver registries).
# Example: RESEARCHER_DATA_CARVEOUTS=api/src/ingest/resolver_data/pubs.yaml
# RESEARCHER_DATA_CARVEOUTS=

# =============================================================================
# Runtime secrets / project-specific (fill as your project requires)
# =============================================================================
# DATABASE_URL=...
# API_KEY=...
# (add what your application needs; this section is not framework-managed)

# =============================================================================
# Git auth auto-wire (FWADR-030) — executes when this .env is sourced
# =============================================================================
# Routes `git` over HTTPS to the declared host's CLI credential helper, using
# the token above. Session-scoped: it exports GIT_CONFIG_* for this shell only
# and writes NOTHING to any gitconfig, so it lives and dies with the terminal
# and never leaks between projects. Host-neutral by construction — the github
# and gitlab branches are mirrors, and GIT_HOST_URL makes self-hosted (GitHub
# Enterprise / self-managed GitLab) first-class on both, exactly as gitlab.com /
# github.com are the unset-URL defaults.
#
# Requires HTTPS remotes: for an SSH remote (git@host:...) the helper never
# engages and auth falls back to keys via ~/.ssh/config — which is correct, and
# fails loudly (not silently) if misconfigured. No-op when GIT_HOST is
# PLACEHOLDER/other. Single declared host per project; a mixed-host multi-repo
# project extends GIT_CONFIG_COUNT by hand.
case "$GIT_HOST" in
  github)
    _host="${GIT_HOST_URL:-https://github.com}"
    [ -n "$GIT_HOST_URL" ] && export GH_HOST="${GIT_HOST_URL#http*://}"
    export GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=1 \
           GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0="credential.${_host}.helper" \
           GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0='!gh auth git-credential'
    unset _host ;;
  gitlab)
    _host="${GIT_HOST_URL:-https://gitlab.com}"
    [ -n "$GIT_HOST_URL" ] && export GITLAB_HOST="${GIT_HOST_URL#http*://}"
    export GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=1 \
           GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0="credential.${_host}.helper" \
           GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0='!glab auth git-credential'
    unset _host ;;
esac
